[ti:Becoming the Flame]
[ar:EdgarAllanMusic]
[al:EcceH.text (Revalued)]
[00:04.11]The fact that one becomes what one is
[00:06.86]Presupposes that one has not the remotest suspicion of what one is
[00:12.78]
[00:33.29]In the mirror, broken days
[00:38.36]I watched my shadow thin
[00:44.09]A twisted soul in borrowed flame
[00:49.47]The poison folded in
[00:54.85]Every scar became a map
[00:57.58]Every fall a place to stand
[01:00.14]I let the saint inside me die
[01:03.12]A satyr took my hand
[01:05.42]Nobody told me where I'm going
[01:10.89]Nothing in me knew the way
[01:14.27]I become what I am
[01:16.64]Without a map or aim
[01:19.46]A spark that never asked
[01:22.15]The meaning of the flame
[01:27.01]
[01:34.44]Thirty-six, a lamp turned low, I couldn't read three steps away
[01:37.00]The age my father faded at and I was fading the same way
[01:39.96]In my father I'm already gone, in my mother I grow old
[01:42.91]A decadent and a beginning, I'm the ember and the cold
[01:45.67]Shadow summer, sunless winter, every curtain drawn for good
[01:48.43]But the sickness taught me tasting, little things the way I should
[01:51.18]Bread and weather, wind and window, light that crawls across the floor
[01:54.01]I got well because I wanted, and I wanted nothing more
[01:57.34]Nobody told me who I'd be
[02:02.42]The fever wrote it down for me
[02:08.42]I become what I am
[02:11.36]Half the dusk and half the dawn
[02:14.16]A spark that never asked
[02:16.85]Which side it's burning on
[02:19.61]I traded thorns for vines
[02:22.37]Let the ivy find my brow
[02:24.82]And I screamed yes — not to a fight —
[02:27.69]To all of it, then and now
[02:31.83]Not a hero. Never was
[02:36.52]Just a fever that learned to sing
[02:41.87]I become what I am
[02:44.29]Without a map or aim
[02:47.00]A spark that never asked
[02:49.61]The meaning of the flame
[02:53.97]
[03:01.12]...and I never knew what I am
[03:02.82]
